1. A transportation system (100) for transporting large items (2), the transportation system (100) comprising:  

- at least two longitudinal girders (10) extending in a longitudinal direction of the transportation system (100);  
- a plurality of pairs of transversal primary support beams (20), each pair comprising two transversal primary support beams (20) extending transversely between and/or across the longitudinal girders (10);  
- at least one storage area (30) for receiving at least one large item (2), the storage area (30) being defined longitudinally between two adjacent pairs of transversal primary support beams (20); and  
- lower locking features (40) arranged on a lower side of the transportation system (100),  

characterised in that the lower locking features (40) are positioned and configured to cooperate with standard freight-container locking devices, in particular twist-lock devices, such that the transportation system (100) is lockable to freight-container-compatible transport or handling equipment.
